{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789405806,"nonce":"ly3R3zoI28nxqYKT6CxDxuDagKw=","title":"SSA: an if-expression initialising a let inside a loop body adds a phi incoming from a block that is not a predecessor","message":"In the built-in library's DSL, a loop body containing\n\n    let mid = if lo + w \u003c n { lo + w } else { n };\n\n(a `TypedExpression::If` as the initialiser of a `let`, inside a\n`while`) lowered to a phi at the inner loop's header with an incoming\nfrom the block the `let` sits in, which is not a predecessor of the\nheader once the if-expression has split it. Cranelift then rejects the\nfunction: \"brif ... mismatched argument count: got 0, expected 1\", and\nthe tiered backend skips the body, which surfaces at run time as\n\"can't resolve symbol zb_list_sort_by_i64\".\n\nReproduce by writing `merge_sort` in `zyntax_builtins/src/lists.rs`\nwith `if_expr` for the `mid`/`hi` bounds instead of the `when`\nstatements it uses now; the dumped HIR of `zb_list_sort_i64` shows the\nphi (`%v41: i64 = phi [.., block6], ..` on a block whose preds do not\ninclude block6). Same family as 19c227b and the continuation-block\nprotocol notes.","files":null}]}